{
  "id": "latin-square",
  "term": "Latin square",
  "definition": "A Latin square is a block design used to arrange different test conditions across participants rather than giving everyone the same condition order. In this source, it refers to assigning different background conditions in a between-subjects way, which meant participants did not receive directly comparable tests or scores.",
